    <statement><p>Find <m>3 + 6 + 12 + \cdots + 3\cdot 2^{18}\text{.}</m></p>
<p><fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{786432\cdot 2-3}{1}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p><m>\frac{3\cdot 2^{19}-3}{1}\text{.}</m>  Let the sum be <m>S\text{,}</m> and compute <m>2S - S = 1S\text{,}</m> which causes terms except <m>3</m> and <m>3\cdot 2^{19}</m> to cancel.  Then solve for <m>S\text{.}</m></p>
</solution>
